messages:
maria: Quick async check — planning a canary for the new client-side header gate. want to validate audience + fallback behavior before i flip anything.
sam: sg. which header again? and what's the goal audience %? :eyes:
maria: header is `x-redwood-client-info` with `ver` field. goal: enable feature for 5% of web + mobile clients on >=1.4.0, keep older clients default-off. also need telemetry to detect malformed headers.
rahul: sounds right. pls ensure server-side version parse is defensive — clients sometimes send `1.4` vs `1.4.0`.
jess: are we doing header-only gating or also client-id targeting? For the first canary i'd prefer header+audience to reduce noise.
maria: header+audience. rollout plan:
- create flag `client_gate_v2_header` off by default
- lift to 5% for clients reporting `ver >= 1.4.0`
- for clients without header, treat as older -> opt-out
- add metric `client_gate_v2.malformed_header` and `client_gate_v2.fallback_used`
- alert if error rate or latency spikes >2x baseline
sam: can you paste the minimal header parsing snippet you want us to use? i'll add it to SDK PR.
maria: sure — implementation sketch:
```
// pseudo
const info = req.headers['x-redwood-client-info'] || '';
// expected: "ver=1.4.2;os=ios"
const parsed = parseKvString(info); // tolerant parse
const clientVer = normalizeVersion(parsed.ver);
if (!clientVer) {
  metrics.increment('client_gate_v2.malformed_header');
  useOldBehavior();
} else if (versionGte(clientVer, '1.4.0')) {
  checkFlag('client_gate_v2_header', userId);
} else {
  metrics.increment('client_gate_v2.fallback_used');
  useOldBehavior();
}
```
olivia: for SDKs: we'll need a small compatibility shim — older SDKs should continue sending the old `x-redwood-sdk` header; new SDKs send `x-redwood-client-info`. Server should prefer `x-redwood-client-info` but fall back to `x-redwood-sdk` parsing.
rahul: agree. also add a deploy-bot annotation to the rollout: include canary group id so infra can route if needed.
deploy-bot: Canary configured: flag=client_gate_v2_header, audience=clients>=1.4.0, percent=5, id=canary-2026-03-17-01
jess: Can someone own the PR review and the observability dashboard? I'll own telemetry dashboards if @sam adds the metric names to the PR.
sam: i'll pick up the SDK PR + server header parsing change. will add tests for `1.4`, `1.4.0`, and malformed.
maria: awesome. checklist for rollout:
- [ ] server parsing + metrics (sam)
- [ ] SDK shim + opt-in header (olivia)
- [ ] flag created and canary configured (maria/deploy-bot)
- [ ] dashboard + alerts (jess)
- [ ] short smoke run on staging with simulated older clients (rahul)

rahul: Q: do we need an escape hatch? e.g., immediate global kill switch?
maria: yes — the flag itself is global kill switch. ops: add runbook to page with steps: rollback flag, check prefix cache flush, revert client target if needed.
olivia: also add client-side gate to only attempt new header if SDK has seen server OK once; prevents endless errors for older infra.
sam: will tag reviewers in PR: @jess @olivia @maria — expect draft by EOD PST.
maria: thanks — post any blockers here. i'll start the flag creation flow now and attach canary id.
deploy-bot: Canary update: canary-2026-03-17-01 -> active
jess: noted. once metrics look stable at 5% for 24h, we'll plan progressive increase to 25% with a followup thread.
maria: perfect. pfps for PRs and this thread: tag me for the final go/no-go. :thumbsup:
